# nightpost — runtime configuration
#
# The Go binary reads NO environment variables at runtime: everything is CLI
# flags on cmd/monitor. This file documents the deployment-facing knobs;
# nothing here is sourced automatically — translate them into the compose /
# Dokploy service definition (or a wrapper script) instead.
#
# Ingest contract: see WIRE_SPEC.md (frozen) and testdata/wire/ (executable).
#   POST /ingest/{project}/sentry|profile|error|xhprof|query|job|release
#   POST /api/{project}/store|envelope        (Sentry SDK compatibility)
#   POST /api/profiler/store                  (spiral-packages/profiler)
#   TCP 9913                                  (Monolog newline-JSON)
#   GET  /up                                  (liveness — never checks the DB)
#   GET  /ready                               (readiness — does check the DB)
#
# Flag              Default     Meaning
# ----------------- ----------- -------------------------------------------------
# -db               monitor.db  SQLite path — mount a PERSISTENT volume; single
#                               instance only (no replicas).
# -http             :8000       UI + all HTTP ingest.
# -socket           :9913       Monolog TCP socket.
# -retention-days   30          Occurrences older than this are pruned in the
#                               background (chunked deletes; issues kept).
# -prune-interval   10m         Retention cycle frequency.
# -occurrence-cap   30          Max occurrence rows per issue per minute
#                               (0 = unlimited).
# -session-secret   (random)    HMAC key for dashboard session cookies.
# -session-secret-file          File holding that key. Loaded when
#                               -session-secret is empty; a GENERATED key is
#                               written there (0600), so restarts keep logins.
#                               The shipped image sets this to
#                               /data/session.key. Without either, the key is
#                               random per boot and every deploy logs admins out.
# -cookie-secure    false       Mark the session cookie Secure. SET THIS when
#                               TLS terminates at a reverse proxy: the
#                               connection here is plain HTTP, so it cannot be
#                               detected. Never inferred from X-Forwarded-Proto.
# -cors-origin      (empty)     Seed for a project whose browser-origin
#                               allowlist is empty. The PER-PROJECT allowlist
#                               lives on the project row — edit it at /keys.
#                               A wildcard is refused.
# -require-registered   false   Refuse an ingest POST naming a project nobody
#                               registered (401 unknown project) instead of
#                               auto-provisioning it. SET THIS once ingest is
#                               reachable through a public ingress: it stops the
#                               caller-chosen {project} name being a resource an
#                               attacker allocates. A project that already
#                               exists without a key stays admitted, so flipping
#                               it cannot break a running producer. The product
#                               build defaults it ON at fork time.
# -require-ingest-keys  false   Refuse unsigned ingest outright on projects that
#                               HAVE a key. Also SET THIS on a public ingress.
# -max-auto-projects    500     How many unsigned projects may be
#                               auto-provisioned at all (0 = unbounded).
# -ingest-rate      50          Per-project ingest budget, events/s.
# -ingest-burst     100         Per-project burst ceiling.
# -ingress-global-rate   500    Ceiling across ALL projects (a DoS ceiling, not a
#                               fairness limit — keep it well above real volume).
# -ingress-global-burst  1000
# -ingress-ip-rate      100     Per source address. SET 0 BEHIND A PROXY, where
#                               every request shares the proxy address.
# -ingress-ip-burst     200
# -reset-admin      (empty)     One-shot recovery: create/re-key this email and
#                               write a fresh password to a 0600 file, then
#                               exit. It is NEVER printed to the log.
# -reset-admin-out              Where that password goes (default
#                               <db-dir>/admin-reset.txt).
# -alerts-config    (empty)     JSON channels+rules file (mounted secret).
#                               Empty = alerting fully disabled, zero cost.
#
# Example compose command:
#   command: ["/usr/local/bin/monitor", "-db", "/data/monitor.db",
#             "-http", ":8000", "-socket", ":9913",
#             "-session-secret-file", "/data/session.key", "-cookie-secure"]
#   volumes:  [monitor-data:/data]
#
# Full exposure checklist and upgrade notes: DEPLOY.md.
#
# The PRODUCERS live in the client projects, not here — their env keys are
# documented in fenrirealm-backend/.env.example (MONITOR_*, XHPROF_ENABLED,
# PROFILER_ENDPOINT, SENTRY_LARAVEL_DSN) and fenrirealm-front/.env.example.
